{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})+1)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-8845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "With $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})+1) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{vx}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{vx}{x})+1) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =v(\\operatorname{ln}⁡v+1) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v \\\\ \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo evaluate the integral on the left-hand side, we use integration by substitution with\n\n$$\nu=\\operatorname{ln}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=\\frac{1}{v}.\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{u}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡v| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡v| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{C} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{C}|x|) \\\\ |\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =|x|{e}^{C} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x} & =\\pm {e}^{C}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x} & =Kx \\\\ \\frac{y}{x} & ={e}^{Kx} \\\\ y & =x{e}^{Kx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced the new constant of integration:\n\n$$\nK=\\pm {e}^{C}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-8845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64450a22ac35f57be9a9ddce672865b5c0c8bb75bd96b5685d3e7b9feaa70ebd"} {"question" "q-8845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-8845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K(2+{e}^{3x})"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{x}"] ["math" "y=K{x}^{2}+{e}^{x}"] ["math" "y=x{e}^{Kx}"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}+{e}^{Kx}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-8845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=x{e}^{Kx}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{yx}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "With $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{yx}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)x}{(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{v{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{v}+\\frac{1}{{v}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}v & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{2{v}^{2}} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =C \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64450a22ac35f57be9a9ddce672865b5c0c8bb75bd96b5685d3e7b9feaa70ebd"} {"question" "q-14318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}|+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}=C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}=C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}|+2\\frac{y}{x}=C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}=C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{y}{x}=C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}=C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is NOT a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is NOT the case is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}.$\n\nWe see that the numerator is NOT a homogeneous polynomial. Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is NOT a homogeneous function.\n\nHence, the original differential equation is  NOT homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}\\,\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is not homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)\\ne f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\nFor $x=1$, $y=2$ and $t=3$, for instance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =f(2\\cdot 1,2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =f(2,6) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}+1}{{6}^{2}+2(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{48}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =f(1,2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}+1}{{2}^{2}+1(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, there exists at least one combination of values of $x$, $y$ and $t$ for which the identity $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y)$ is not observed.\n\nHence, the original differential equation is  NOT homogeneous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64450a22ac35f57be9a9ddce672865b5c0c8bb75bd96b5685d3e7b9feaa70ebd"} {"question" "q-14322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{x}^{2}y}{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x+y}{y})"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+2y{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+2y{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+x(vx)^{2}-(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+2(vx){x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}(1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3})}{{x}^{3}({v}^{2}+2v)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}-{v}^{3}-2{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+2v}{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64450a22ac35f57be9a9ddce672865b5c0c8bb75bd96b5685d3e7b9feaa70ebd"} {"question" "q-14323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1-2v-3{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+2v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x"] ["math" "\\frac{v+2}{1-3v-2{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{{v}^{2}+2v}{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{{v}^{2}-1}{1-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{{v}^{3}+2{v}^{2}}{1-{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-14323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{v}^{2}+2v}{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-90601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{x}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}).\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-90601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{x}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{vx}{x}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{vx}{x}) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =v-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-90601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64450a22ac35f57be9a9ddce672865b5c0c8bb75bd96b5685d3e7b9feaa70ebd"} {"question" "q-90601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd57200"} {"question" "q-90601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{1}{v}))\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{v-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2}{x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063831/state.json" "file_sha256" "92f11599006ea5536172c8c529e7feb16e46851880850a0b66a0aa27bbd5720